        "question_text": "<p>Find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ if $y = x^3 \\ln x$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the product rule: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = u \\frac{dv}{dx} + v \\frac{du}{dx}$, where $u = x^3$ and $v = \\ln x$.<br>$\\frac{du}{dx} = 3x^2$, $\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{dy}{dx} = x^3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + \\ln x \\cdot 3x^2 = x^2 + 3x^2 \\ln x$.</p>",
